{"id": "6225fda09acc5376d4870dda", "name": "Financial Services Sector Cyber Threat Intel - Key Insights (February 2022)", "description": "In February, an APT10 espionage group, believed to be from China, was linked to attacks on a local financial sector. The attacks started at the end of November 2021 and continued till February. The intrusions were tracked under the codename of Operation Cache Panda.\n\nOther Major Incidents\nUsers of Monzo were targeted by phishing messages supported by a growing network of malicious websites. The BlackByte ransomware group targeted three organizations (including a financial entity) based in the U.S. An Antlion APT group was found to be using the 'xPack' backdoor against financial organizations. Medusa malware distributed through SMiShing service, named Cabassous and known for targeting the financial organizations in Turkey. LendUS discovered and then fixed a security incident.", "author_name": "SVThreatIntel", "modified": "2022-04-06T00:02:16.312000", "created": "2022-03-07T12:42:08.232000", "tags": ["apt10 sha1", "monzo domains", "antlion apt", "sha256", "Financial Services"], "references": [], "public": 1, "adversary": "Informational", "targeted_countries": [], "malware_families": [], "attack_ids": [], "industries": [], "TLP": "white", "indicators": [{"id": 3381537816, "indicator": "91.212.150.0/24", "type": "CIDR", "created": "2022-03-07T12:42:09", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 3381537817, "indicator": "93.157.62.0/24", "type": "CIDR", "created": "2022-03-07T12:42:09", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 3381537818, "indicator": "93.157.63.0/24", "type": "CIDR", "created": "2022-03-07T12:42:09", "content": "", "title": "", "description": "", "expiration": null, "is_active": 1}, {"id": 3376928395, "indicator": "0c7b8da133799dd72d0dbe3ea012031e", "type": "FileHash-MD5", "created": "2022-03-07T12:42:09", "content": 